course: dictionary
lesson: 458
title: Armadillo: a word from the animal world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An armadillo is a small mammal from the Americas. Its body is covered in hard, bony plates that work like armour, so it is well protected. Armour is a useful clue word here: if you know what armour is, you can guess what the plates do.
explain: «Armadillo armour is made of bone plates covered with tough skin.» The words «bone plates» and «tough skin» tell you what the armour is made from. Read the sentence again and find the clue words before you check a dictionary.
explain: Armadillos dig for insects with their strong claws. «The armadillo dug with strong claws to find insects to eat.» You can work out that claws are sharp, strong parts of the body that help an animal dig.
explain: Some words come from other languages. The name armadillo is Spanish for «little armoured one». When you meet a new word, ask what it could mean, then check your idea in the sentence.
fact: An armadillo is a small mammal from the Americas.
fact: Armadillos have bony plates on their bodies that work like armour.
fact: Armadillos use their strong claws to dig for insects.
fact: Only the three-banded armadillo can roll fully into a ball.
fact: The nine-banded armadillo almost always has four identical babies.
exercise: «The nine-banded armadillo almost always has four identical babies.» What does identical mean? | Covered in hair | *Exactly the same | Small and quiet | Very hungry
exercise: «Armadillo armour is made of bone plates covered with tough skin.» What is the armour made of? | Glass | Hair | Feathers | *Bone plates
exercise: «The armadillo dug with strong claws to find insects to eat.» What did the armadillo use to dig? | Its ears | *Its claws | Its tail | A spade
test: The name armadillo is Spanish for «little armoured one». What does this name tell you about the animal? | *Armadillos have a hard, armour-like covering | Armadillos can fly high in the sky | Armadillos live in water | Armadillos have no legs
test: «Only the three-banded armadillo can roll fully into a ball.» Which armadillo can do this? | The giant armadillo, which is in a different group | *The three-banded armadillo | Every armadillo, and no others | The nine-banded armadillo
exam: Which words best describe an armadillo's body? | Smooth and shiny like glass | Soft and feathery | Covered in scales like a fish | *Covered in hard, bony plates
